ily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Richmond has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Richmond has warmed, days and nights alike","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 56\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>56\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 61\u00b0F, and the record is 81\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>41\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Richmond has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Richmond's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Richmond has set <strong class=\"sig\">20 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 76 that chance alone would give, and <strong>93 record highs</strong>, close to the 76 that chance alone would give. The 1950s hold the most record highs of any decade (45). Richmond's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on August 6, 1918.","t_chg":"Richmond has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 129 complete years: Richmond's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.12\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.05 to +0.18), about +1.5\u00b0F since 1897. Richmond's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.23\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.29), about +2.9\u00b0F since 1897.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in 9 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Richmond's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.22 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 45.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1889 (72.02 in); the driest, 1941 (22.91 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}